meta {
  name: Bulk Assign
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/assignments/bulk
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "lead_ids": ["{{leadId}}"],
    "assigned_to": "{{userId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Hands several leads to one user in a single action. Backs the Bulk Assign
  screen. Requires the `lms.leads.assign.bulk` capability.

  Rules enforced server-side:
    - every lead in lead_ids must belong to the SAME branch
    - the assignee must belong to that same branch
    - canAssignToUser rank check still applies

  A caller whose `lms.leads.view` scope is tenant/all runs under the tenant
  Postgres role, so they can act on a branch other than their session branch —
  which is what lets a tenant admin pick a branch in the UI and assign within
  it. Everyone else stays pinned to their own branch by RLS.

  Response: { success: true, data: { updated: <n>, skipped: [<lead_id>, ...] } }
  `skipped` holds leads already assigned to that same user.
}
